                    {
                        "form_id": "7c978177-0d55-40de-8ee0-9671fe752ff0",
                        "entry_id": "0b205eef-b31d-38f9-9e34-cfba3f45195d",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "catechized"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c3f37ed9-cc7a-3305-aacc-d2e31d56e529",
                        "entry_id": "0b205eef-b31d-38f9-9e34-cfba3f45195d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To give oral instruction, especially of religion; (specifically) by the formal question-and-answer method; in the Church of England and Roman Catholic Church, to teach the catechism as preparation for confirmation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9b1687de-b461-3263-bea7-16f0e055518e",
                        "entry_id": "0b205eef-b31d-38f9-9e34-cfba3f45195d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To question at length."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "51d5eda3-bbaf-42d6-b84a-1a5f316f08d7",
                                "sense_id": "9b1687de-b461-3263-bea7-16f0e055518e",
                                "text": "She promised herself to ascertain thoroughly, after they should be comfortably settled in the ship, the animus with which the book was to be written. She was a very good sailor and she liked to talk at sea; there her husband would not be able to escape from her, and she foresaw the manner in which she should catechise him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "524cfbe1-c076-44c0-aba1-403bfe700e6b",
                                "sense_id": "9b1687de-b461-3263-bea7-16f0e055518e",
                                "text": "Putting a strong American inflection into the French which I usually talked with an unmistakable British accent, I catechised the Baron as to the date of the church's building, its dimensions, and other details which an American tourist would be certain to want to know."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0a831d00-bca4-4f43-b4bf-2cbd4aba3c00",
                        "source_entry_id": "0b205eef-b31d-38f9-9e34-cfba3f45195d",
                        "source_sense_description": "give oral instruction, especially of religion",
                        "target_lang_word": "catéchiser",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "catéchiser",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31bc3f11-d70c-3b8e-be66-e05df58cff40",
                                        "entry_id": "bb211b38-1b66-3f90-8675-a5b7bb8d966f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Instruire des principaux points de la religion chrétienne."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bffe60e8-c0ef-4217-879f-5c4c3f2861cc",
                                                "sense_id": "31bc3f11-d70c-3b8e-be66-e05df58cff40",
                                                "text": "Il avait marié les vieux, baptisé les jeunes, enterré les aïeuls, catéchisé des générations de moutards, […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11e68c04-bac5-3947-bbb2-9a705c916349",
                                        "entry_id": "bb211b38-1b66-3f90-8675-a5b7bb8d966f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tâcher de persuader quelque chose à quelqu’un, lui dire toutes les raisons qui peuvent l’engager à faire une chose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d48c78f-a233-41d6-a33d-e45e5e663a19",
                                                "sense_id": "11e68c04-bac5-3947-bbb2-9a705c916349",
                                                "text": "Je l’ai longtemps catéchisé, mais inutilement. — Il faut un peu le catéchiser."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49878415-ab9f-4fe9-8ed5-ffe628f7db70",
                                                "sense_id": "11e68c04-bac5-3947-bbb2-9a705c916349",
                                                "text": "Son parent, M. de Valqueyras, lui ayant défendu d’introduire des affiliés dans son hôtel, il avait choisi le salon jaune de Félicité. D’ailleurs, il ne tarda pas à trouver dans Pierre un aide précieux. Il ne pouvait aller prêcher lui-même la cause de la légitimité aux petits détaillants et aux ouvriers du vieux quartier ; on l’aurait hué. Pierre, au contraire, qui avait vécu au milieu de ces gens-là, parlait leur langue, connaissait leurs besoins, arrivait à les catéchiser en douceur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c77f03b7-dc02-42e3-a0af-2a99351170a1",
                                                "sense_id": "11e68c04-bac5-3947-bbb2-9a705c916349",
                                                "text": "Faire apprendre sans comprendre ce qu’on devrait comprendre. C’est un des sens populaires du mot « catéchiser »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
